# Trivy IaC misconfiguration suppressions.
#
# Each entry is an intentional, accepted-risk design decision for this
# architecture, not a scanner error. New findings outside this list still
# gate the build (severity: HIGH,CRITICAL).
# Reference: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/

# Unrestricted egress to any IP (ECS task/service security groups).
# Outbound access is required for the tasks to reach AWS APIs, pull images,
# and call external services (Stripe, Discord, OAuth providers).
AWS-0104

# Public ALB. The load balancer is intentionally internet-facing — it fronts
# the public API/frontend.
AWS-0053

# CloudFront distribution without an attached WAF. Accepted for now; WAF is
# not part of the current design.
AWS-0011

# ECR image tags are mutable. Accepted for the current deploy workflow.
AWS-0031

# S3 public access block does not block public policies, and does not
# restrict public buckets. These fire only on the public images bucket
# (modules/s3_public_images), which must serve objects publicly by design.
AWS-0087
AWS-0093

# S3 buckets use SSE-S3 (AES256) rather than a customer-managed KMS key.
# Accepted: AES256 at-rest encryption is in place; CMK is not required here.
AWS-0132
